title: Pick entities in the Inspector
intro: Fields that name another entity now list the scene's entities to pick from, and take one dragged from the Hierarchy.
project: Platformer | Entity Pickers

chapter: Pick from the scene | A list by every field that names an entity
select: Lever
say: This lever brings out the bridge. Its Targets field names what it turns on.
explain: pick:Switch.Targets | The entity list | Fields that name entities now have a button that lists everything in the scene, laid out like the Hierarchy.
say: Let's have the lever start the lift too. The lift sits inside the Level group, so it's indented under it.
pickentity: Switch.Targets = Lift
expectvalue: Lever.Switch.Targets = Bridge, Lift
explain: field:Switch.Targets | Added, not replaced | Targets names several things, so picking one adds it to the list, with the comma put in for you.
say: Picking one that's already ticked takes it out again.
pickentity: Switch.Targets = Lift
expectvalue: Lever.Switch.Targets = Bridge
say: No more typing names and hoping they match.

chapter: Drag from the Hierarchy | Drop an entity on the field
select: Main Camera
explain: field:Follow.Target | Follows the player | The camera follows whatever its Target names: the player.
say: Drag the slime's row from the Hierarchy onto the field.
dropentity: Slime > Follow.Target
expectvalue: Main Camera.Follow.Target = Slime
expectselected: Main Camera
explain: panel:Inspector | Still on the camera | Pressing on a row to drag it doesn't select it, so the Inspector stays on the camera you're editing.
play
wait: 3
explain: game | Following the slime | Now the camera rides along with the slime.
stop
dropentity: Player > Follow.Target
expectvalue: Main Camera.Follow.Target = Player
say: Drag the player back, and it's as it was. Every pick and drop is one undo step.
